{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents.</b> The poet's words speak in the voice of Israel in exile." "<b>Greatly.</b> I have explained it." "<b>Let Israel now say.</b> By way of prophecy, for thus he will say 'greatly' time after time. And the meaning: even though adversaries, they will not be able to blot out their remembrance."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 129, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:25.738882714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}